---
import '@fontsource/instrument-serif/400.css';
import '@fontsource/instrument-serif/400-italic.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/500.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/600.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/500.css';
import BaseHead from '../../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import CoffeeDoctor from '../../../components/coffee/CoffeeDoctor.svelte';
import { SYMPTOMS, SOURCES } from '../../../lib/coffee/index.ts';

const title = 'Fix My Coffee: Why It Tastes Sour, Bitter or Weak';
const description = 'Say how you brewed and what tastes wrong. Two or three quick questions find the likely cause and give you one change to make in your next brew.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
			'@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebApplication', name: 'Fix My Coffee',
			url: 'https://jayarr.coffee/tools/fix-my-coffee/', description, applicationCategory: 'UtilityApplication', operatingSystem: 'Any',
			offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' }, publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'JayArr Coffee', url: 'https://jayarr.coffee' },
		})}></script>
	</head>
	<body class="cf-page">
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="cf-intro">
				<a href="/tools/" class="cf-back">← All tools</a>
				<p class="cf-kicker">Fix My Coffee</p>
				<h1>Why does my coffee taste <em>sour, bitter or weak?</em></h1>
				<p class="cf-lede">Say how you brewed it and what tastes wrong. A couple of quick questions tell the causes apart, and you get one change to make next time.</p>
			</section>
			<section class="cf-tool" aria-label="Fix My Coffee"><CoffeeDoctor client:load /></section>

			<article class="cf-body">
				<h2>Sour or bitter: which way to go</h2>
				<p>Coffee's compounds dissolve at different speeds, so the taste changes as more of the coffee is extracted. Under-extracted cups tend to taste sour and thin, and over-extracted ones bitter and drying. A <strong>sour</strong> cup usually stopped too early (under-extracted): grind finer or use hotter water. A <strong>bitter</strong> cup usually went too far (over-extracted): grind coarser or use cooler water. Change one thing at a time, and change it a little.</p>
				<p>You'll often read that acids dissolve first, then sugars, then bitter compounds. That tidy order is a simplification: the bitter, slow end is better supported than the sour, fast one, and UC Davis researchers propose that coffee's sweet impression comes mostly from aroma and low bitterness, not dissolved sugar. Our <a href="/deep-brew/research/extraction-sequence-explained/">note on the extraction sequence</a> sets out what has been measured.</p>
				<p>The brew time is a useful clue. If a V60 finishes in two minutes instead of three to four, the grind is likely too coarse. For a conventional shot, an espresso that runs in fifteen seconds instead of twenty-five to thirty is likely ground too coarse; turbo shots run that fast on purpose.</p>

				<h2>Weak is a different problem</h2>
				<p>Strength is how much coffee is dissolved in the cup; extraction is how much was pulled out of the grounds. A cup can be well extracted and still weak, because there simply wasn't enough coffee for the water. Weak means use more coffee for the same water, not a finer grind. The <a href="/tools/brew-ratio/">Brew Guide</a> gives you the grams for your cup.</p>

				<h2>When it tastes sour and bitter at once</h2>
				<p>That usually means uneven extraction: some grounds over-extracted while others were bypassed. Blade grinders cause it by making dust and boulders together, and so does water channeling through a pour-over bed or an espresso puck. Even out the grind and the bed before chasing the dial.</p>

				<h2>What it asks about</h2>
				<ul>
					{SYMPTOMS.map((s) => <li><strong>{s.label}</strong>: {s.tagline.toLowerCase()}.</li>)}
				</ul>
				<p>Want to see where your cup sits between sour and bitter, weak and strong? Try the <a href="/deep-brew/extraction/">Extraction Map</a>.</p>

				<h2>Related guides</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><a href="/blog/coffee-extraction-yield-explained/">Extraction yield explained</a></li>
					<li><a href="/blog/why-coffee-tastes-bitter-how-to-fix/">Why coffee tastes bitter</a></li>
					<li><a href="/blog/how-to-dial-in-espresso/">How to dial in espresso</a></li>
					<li><a href="/blog/fix-channeling-uneven-extraction/">Fixing channeling and uneven extraction</a></li>
					<li><a href="/tools/grind-guide/">Grind Guide</a></li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Sources</h2>
				<ul class="cf-sources">
					{['gagne', 'rao', 'sca-chart', 'nguyen-phin', 'synthesis'].map((id) => SOURCES[id]).map((s) => <li>{s.author}, <cite>{s.title}</cite>{s.year ? ` (${s.year})` : ''}{s.where ? `: ${s.where}` : ''}.</li>)}
				</ul>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style is:global>.cf-page { background: #f3ede3; }</style>
<style>
	main { color: #2a1d15; }
	.cf-intro { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 120px 24px 22px; }
	.cf-back { font: 500 12px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', 'IBM Plex Mono Metrics', monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #75655a; text-decoration: none; }
	.cf-kicker { font: 500 12px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', 'IBM Plex Mono Metrics', monospace; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #8f5d22; margin: 26px 0 0; }
	h1 { font: 400 clamp(40px, 6vw, 68px)/.98 'Instrument Serif', 'Instrument Serif Metrics', Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 10px 0 12px; }
	h1 em { font-style: italic; color: #7a4e30; }
	.cf-lede { font: 400 17px/1.5 'IBM Plex Sans', 'IBM Plex Sans Metrics', system-ui, sans-serif; color: #5b4a3d; max-width: 36em; /* 60ch of Plex */ margin: 0; }
	.cf-tool { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 8px 24px 40px; }
	.cf-body { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 24px 72px; font: 400 17px/1.7 'IBM Plex Sans', 'IBM Plex Sans Metrics', system-ui, sans-serif; }
	.cf-body h2 { font: 400 34px/1.1 'Instrument Serif', 'Instrument Serif Metrics', Georgia, serif; margin: 44px 0 12px; }
	.cf-body a { color: #7a4e30; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
	.cf-sources { font-size: 14.5px; color: #5b4a3d; }
	@media (max-width: 640px) { .cf-intro { padding: 96px 16px 18px; } .cf-tool { padding: 4px 12px 32px; } .cf-body { padding: 16px 16px 56px; } }
</style>
